                     <provenance type="#s l" source="4947"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_484"
                           >Salisbury, Wiltshire. Cathedral church of St Mary the Virgin; see
                           removed from Sherborne in 1078</orgName><p>Compare Henderson,
                              <title>Liber Pontificalis Chr. Bainbridge Archiepiscopi Eboracensis,
                           </title>Surtees Society 61 (1875), pp. xvii-xxx, and Frere,
                              <title>Pontifical Services</title>, Alcuin Club Collections, 1.
                           97–98.</p><p>Form of service for use in the diocese of Salisbury (fol.
                           111v). </p></provenance>
                     <provenance type="#c" cert="low" source="5217"><orgName role="fmo"
                           key="org_499">Sherborne, Dorset. Benedictine abbey of St Mary the Virgin;
                           seat of bishopric until A. D. 1078</orgName><p>Probably in use at
                           Sherborne. The form of profession (fol. 92v) runs <q>Ego frater N
                              sacerdos et diaconus promitto conversionem ... coram deo et sanctis
                              eius in hoc monasterio quod est constructum in honore sancte Marie de
                              Scyreburnia et in presentia domni N. episcopi</q> (see Henderson,
                              <title>Liber Pontificalis Chr. Bainbridge Archiepiscopi
                              Eboracensis</title>, Surtees Society 61 (1875), p.
                        xxvii).</p></provenance>
